          "quote": "(net (name \"COL3\") ... (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_RX+\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"COL4\") ... (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_RX-\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"COL5\") ... (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"9\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT2_RX+\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "netlist shows 5 column + 7 row lines wired directly to SKW92A GPIO pins (matrix scanned by the module itself)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If these module pins are dedicated Ethernet PHY connections rather than GPIO-multiplexable pins, the keyboard columns will not scan correctly and may load or interfere with the Ethernet interfaces. The netlist does not establish whether the module supports GPIO operation on these particular pins, so this finding is conditional on their pin-mux capability.",
      "confidence": 0.76
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The keyboard column nets connect to SKW92A pins identified in the netlist as LAN PHY signals, despite the specification describing them as GPIO scan lines. This is a likely pin-function conflict, although confirmation depends on whether those specific pins support GPIO multiplexing."
}

